  "name": "google-cloud-storage-okf-bucket",
  "description": "Discovers, inventories, triages, and searches across Google Cloud Storage (GCS) buckets and prefixes (gs://bucket or gs://bucket/prefix/) using the Open Knowledge Format (OKF). Aggregates per-object OKF status (fresh, stale, unindexed), Tier 0 summaries, region titles, keywords, and custom contexts in a single metadata listing without downloading object payloads. Use when: (1) answering open-ended discovery, search, or root-cause triage questions across a GCS bucket or prefix; (2) auditing bucket OKF index health and identifying candidates_to_index; (3) comparing sections across multiple objects in a bucket; or (4) batch-indexing unindexed (20 KB or larger) and stale objects across a bucket. Don't use for single-object navigation when the exact gs://bucket/object URI is already known and no bucket-level discovery is needed (use google-cloud-storage-okf), or for bucket provisioning and IAM administration (use google-cloud-storage-basics or google-cloud-storage-bucket-architect).",
